  "readings": [
    "HIGH STILL TRAILS LEAN ON RECALL. High (4B, full width, its calibrated 0.42 floor) finds 31/38 against lean's 33/38: -1 single-hop, -1 multi-hop. Its MRR is higher (0.592 vs 0.569), so what it finds it ranks better.",
    "THE HIGH PROFILE'S SHIPPED WARM DEFAULT IS NOT SUPPORTED HERE. high+rerank (the 0.6B, ON by default in high's warm mode since HCR-4) keeps 31/38 and LOWERS MRR, 0.592 -> 0.573 (single-hop 0.781 -> 0.755, multi-hop 0.455 -> 0.441). HCR-4's evidence showed both rerankers raising MRR on the high index, but that index sat at the 0.50 default floor before HCR-3's 0.42 landed; at 0.42 the result reverses. The explicit 4B reranker is the same: 31/38, MRR 0.570. No default is changed here; this is the owner's call.",
    "THE DEEP POOL CLOSES THE GAP. Reranking the top 30 fused hits before the cut takes high to 34/38 (single-hop 15/16, multi-hop 19/22) \u2014 one row above lean and the only arm above it \u2014 at MRR 0.604. On lean the pool keeps 33/38 and gives the best MRR measured, 0.630. Cost: the pool's in-process median is ~1.7-1.9 s under this load against SERVE_BUDGET_MS 1500, so as measured it does not fit the warm budget; a smaller pool, or the pool only on the explicit surfaces, is the next measurement.",
    "LEAN + RERANK: same 33/38, MRR 0.569 -> 0.619 (+0.050; single-hop +0.052, multi-hop +0.048). The quality case for decision D2 holds; its in-process median was 650 ms under load (p95 1.23 s).",
    "THE PPR WALK OVER HIGH IS STILL FLAT TO WORSE: high+walk 30/38 (-1 multi-hop), MRR 0.592 -> 0.579; with rerank 30/38, MRR 0.567. Per decision D4 the flag retires; that removal is its own change.",
    "MRL WIDTH: KEEP THE NATIVE 2560. At the full-width floor (0.42), 1024 finds 30/38 (MRR 0.598) and 2048 31/38 (MRR 0.578), against full width's 31/38 (MRR 0.592). Neither truncation adds a hit; 1024 loses one. At the 0.50 default floor both truncations are worse still: 1024 finds 28/38 (MRR 0.572) and 2048 31/38 (MRR 0.520). The default is already native, so nothing changes in code; HCR-2's MRL question is settled.",
    "INJECTION COST IS FLAT: every arm injects 578-597 estimated tokens per prompt (lean 597).",
    "MEMORY: the 4B embedder holds 4.15 GB of unified memory and loads in 1.9 s; the 0.6B reranker 0.61 GB in 0.37 s; the 4B reranker 4.15 GB in 0.94 s (warm OS cache; run 1 measured 5.3 s and 5.0 s for the two 4B loads on a colder cache). The bench process itself peaked at 18.3 GB RSS holding four indexes and all three models; a warm server holds one high index, the embedder and the 0.6B.",
    "THE SPAWNED HOOK is unchanged on every profile (it serves the lean index): cold p50 357 ms, p95 938 ms over 8 samples under this load."
